{
  "series_title": "Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood",
  "research_status": "COMPLETE — all 64 episodes of Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood (2009–2010) classified canon/filler/mixed. Sourced from three independently-fetched guides (epicdope.com, SuperHeroJacked, QuoteTheAnime) whose episode-level classifications matched exactly: episode 1 tagged 'anime canon' by all three (canon), episodes 4/9/13/14 as partial filler blending original and manga-adapted content within the same episode (mixed), episode 27 as the series' one pure standalone filler episode (filler), and all 59 remaining episodes as straight manga canon. A fourth guide (aniyume.net) was checked as a cross-reference and discarded — it listed a completely different set of 'filler' episodes (including 37, 48, 49, three of the series' most acclaimed and clearly manga-adapted canon episodes), contradicting all three other independently-agreeing sources as well as well-established fan consensus, so it was treated as unreliable rather than a genuine fourth data point. Corrected 2026-08-25: episode 1 was originally recorded as 'mixed' rather than 'canon', an inconsistency with how this project treats the same 'anime canon' label on every other show (see episode 1's own status_note) — caught during a manual cross-check against an independently-sourced breakdown Andreas found himself. Complete, gap-free, non-overlapping coverage of 1–64 confirmed before writing this file.",
  "citation_sources": [
